Security Risk Manager
Be at the forefront of transforming British Army training.

About us:
At OMNIA® Training, we’ve brought together some of the UK’s most innovative defence training organisations under one powerful mission: to transform the British Army’s training system and create the best-trained Army in the world.
OMNIA are redefining the British Army’s collective training. To do that, we are looking for the best and brightest minds from across the UK. We are backed by British innovation and powered by world-class experts, like you. OMNIA is at the heart of the UK’s bold Land Industrial Strategy.

The Role:
This is more than a job — it’s a mission. You will be part of a high-impact, collaborative environment, where we expect everyone to live the values and standards of the British Army. Every person in our team plays a critical role in delivering OMNIA’s vision; designing, delivering, and transforming collective training so the British Army is ready to fight and win.
You’ll work in a matrix organisation and report operationally through OMNIA Training Design Branch and functionally through the Raytheon UK Engineering Management team. Ultimately, you’ll work for the British Army, championing innovation, and helping shape the future of military collective training.
The Omnia Security Risk Manager role requires a versatile individual who can make effective and highly valued contributions to activities across the project lifecycle in collective training and deployed IT environments.  The candidate is expected to be capable of operating in a technical role working closely with customers and delivery teams; alone and unsupervised if necessary. This position is critical to the successful delivery of the Collective Training Transformation Programme (CTTP), ensuring that training is delivered to meet the British Army’s needs. This role concentrates on Information Assurance and Cyber Security but does not exclude supporting Physical and Personnel security elements.
The successful candidate needs to be able to talk to both technical experts and wider organisational stakeholders, applying a holistic approach to create solutions that will help the Organisation achieve its goals. The candidate must be a team player who can work with a multi-skilled engineering team and the customer community.

Key Responsibilities:
Input, management and dissemination of security risks from across all of OMNIA, and ensuring that security risks are properly reported to all relevant Stakeholders in accordance with the defined governance/assurance model (aligned with MoD Secure by Design).
Supporting the Information Assurance team with the implementation of the MoD Secure by Design methodology;
Ownership and maintenance of artefacts such as: Security Risk Management Plan, Security Risk Register, and Key Security Risk Indicators;
Supporting the development of the necessary Information Assurance artefacts and outcomes which support compliance against the MoD assurance process (NIST 800-30/37/53);
Support Information Assurance based engagements with Partners/suppliers and Authority representatives;
Support and contribute towards Security Working Groups and forums with stakeholders;

Essential Skills and Experience:
Sound experience of Security Risk Management;
Passion for Information Security/Assurance and continuous learning;
Self-motivated, problem solver, organised and in possession of good business acumen;
Dynamic and actively acute to evolving Security Risks and their potential impact to the Programme (technology/schedule/cost);Team player but able to work effectively alone;
Ability to work within a fast-paced environment;
Strong communication skills (i.e. oral, presentation and written) with a collaborative approach to teamwork - able to constructively challenge.
Understanding of simulated environments;
In-depth knowledge of Information Assurance and Cyber Security principles, processes and procedures;
Knowledge of Information Assurance and a typical design lifecycle process;
Knowledge of the MoD Secure by Design framework;
Knowledge of supply chain assurance and the relevant MoD standards & policies;
Ability to interpret and solve complex security issues/challenges through analysis or discussion;
Ability to travel (within the UK);
Security cleared or ability to obtain (SC or above).

Desirable Skills and Experience:
Highly organised, discrete, outcome focussed, with a “can do” attitude.
Comfortable working in a Matrix Management Organisation;
Effectively translate and accurately communicate service/system level security issues and risks to leadership/management;
Previous working relationships with senior leadership (e.g. Delivery Team Security Leads);
Working knowledge of ISO 27001 or equivalent standards;
Knowledge of the UK MoD operating model and procurement process for Defence contracts;
Advising leadership and management on technology evolution, emerging issues, cost & schedule implications;
Forward facing, able to engage with peers/Customers;
Sound understanding of cloud infrastructure environments and technology (e.g. AWS, Azure, Google);Knowledge of the Software Development Lifecycle for applications and services;
Working knowledge of Gov Standard 007: Security, NIST standards (800-30/37/53/161), MITRE ATT&CK, CIS Controls, ISO 27001/5, Def-Stan 05-138, JSP 892, and Industry Security Notices;
Understands security requirements and how to decompose them;
Experience of assessment of systems in non-standard environments (not just IT systems);
Possession of a security qualification such as CISM, CRISC, CISSP, CCSP etc;
Support developing plans and estimates, task execution, project tracking, reporting, and risk identification and mitigation plans.

What we offer:
Be Part of a Ground-breaking Mission
Join the UK’s most advanced defence training alliance, where industry experts converge to push boundaries and deliver excellence.
A Culture Built on Collaboration
Work in an inclusive, high-performing team that celebrates ideas, supports growth, and is laser-focused on delivering results.
Team dynamics
You will be part of a team that works together, across multiple organisations united in one mission.
Work Across Borders, United in Purpose
Operate across organisations with one shared goal - improving capability across all domains.
Drive Innovation
Your voice matters. We champion new ideas, welcome change, and believe in continuous improvement with a growth mind-set.
Shape the Future
Play a crucial role in a long-term, future-facing programme with real-world impact on national defence.
Career Growth & Benefits
Enjoy a strong benefits package, ongoing development opportunities, and clear pathways to progress within a trusted defence industry partner.
OMNIA® Training and its partners are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and identities — what matters is your passion, your expertise, and your dedication to the mission.

